# Open Hope Beacon needs no configuration to run.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` only if you want to change one of the settings
# below. The app works with none of them set: everything a church does in the
# demo lives in the browser, so there is no database to connect, no account
# service to configure, and no key to obtain before you can see it working.
#
# There are deliberately NO backend credentials here. If you connect this app to
# a server of your own, its secrets belong on that server — never in this file,
# because anything the browser can read, every visitor can read. See
# docs/BACKENDS.md.

# --- The update floor (normally blank, and it should stay blank) ---
# The oldest build this deployment still supports. Any copy built before this
# moment gets the insistent update reminder instead of the gentle one. Nobody is
# ever locked out: the reminder can always be put away, and switched off entirely
# in Settings. Blank means no floor, which is the default and the usual state.
# A value later than this deployment's own build is clamped, never obeyed.
#
# Any timestamp Date.parse understands, e.g. 2026-08-06T12:00:00Z. Most hosts
# read environment variables at deploy time, so changing this takes effect on
# the next deploy, not immediately. See docs/UPDATES.md.
BEACON_MIN_BUILD_TIME=
